id: darkened
name: Darkened
kind: conditions
# From Normal to Pitch Black is two Levels and from Blinding four, so four stacks is as
# far as it can ever take anybody. Past that it changes nothing.
maxStacks: 4
# Not a Combat Condition: the entry reduces a Square's Light Level and never names one.
combatCondition: no
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The light around you is snuffed out. Your Light Level is 1 lower per stack.
text: >
  Darkened: the Elemental (Dark) Profile's mark. "Any Squares occupied by Character(s) who
  take Damage from this Attacking Maneuver have their Light Level reduced by 1 Level until
  the start of your next turn."

---

# --- The name is this system's ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The entry lowers a Square's Light Level, and this system has no Squares. The Light Level
# is on the character, set by the player on the Battlefields tab, so the reduction lands on
# the character whose Square it was - the one who took the Damage.
#
# It is a mark rather than a change to that field because it has to run out on the
# attacker's clock ("until the start of YOUR next turn"), and a lowered field would have to
# be raised back past whatever the player set in the meantime. So the field stays the
# player's and `lightLevelOf` reads both: the Level set, less one per stack.
#
# Stacks, one per hit, each with its own clock. Two Dark attacks on the same character
# lower it twice, and each wears off when its own attacker's next turn starts.
#
# No effects of its own: what a Light Level does is in that Level's own file, and this
# changes which file is read.
